# 08 — Semantics and Entities

> **For the agent reading this:** Read `plans/07-geometry-tools` and `plans/07B-geometry-refinements` first (the mesh, holes and their scope rule, ramps, the inspector, isolate, lock and hide). The idea came from `plans/thinking-03-semantics-and-entities`, with older notes in `plans/thinking-01-entities`. This phase gives the geometry meaning, and it makes the agent read less to understand more. It adds:
> - **an outline** as `get_scene`'s default: the top level of the tree with names, descriptions and counts, so the agent zooms in where it needs to, plus `find_nodes` and a short on-demand guide instead of one long set of instructions;
> - **the project library:** project-wide **tags** (`#climbable`) and **skills** (`@telekinesis`), both with descriptions, and the project's **design guide**: a markdown file of goals, rules, common failures and the game's facts, which every project gets a default of. Descriptions and notes can reference tags and skills;
> - **notes:** post-its pinned to a point in the scene, with an open / done status, that the agent can read and act on;
> - **entities:** real prefabs. A definition is a small scene with its own undo history, an **instance** in a scene has only a position, a rotation and a name, and editing a definition changes every instance in every scene. An instance behaves like a group for holes.
>
> The review loop (the agent rendering the scene to check its own work) is phase 09, and the array tool is phase 10. The work is split into small increments (§10). Each one ends with the human ↔ agent loop still working and a browser checklist for Orlando. Add this phase's terms to `GLOSSARY.md` (marked "from 08") as they land. Log progress in a §13 at the end of this file, as 07 did.

