## 2. Scope

### In

- **The outline (08.1):**
  - `get_scene` returns one level of the tree by default, with groups summarized, and takes `root`, `depth` and `full`;
  - `find_nodes`;
  - compact JSON;
  - a `description` on groups;
  - the MCP instructions cut to a core, with `get_guide(topic)` for the details.
- **The library (08.2):**
  - tags and skills, with names, descriptions and (for skills) tags;
  - the design guide, in `rules/design-guide.md`, with a default for every project;
  - `tags` on groups and shapes;
  - `@skill` and `#tag` references in any description or note, with autocomplete and highlighting in the editor;
  - aliases on rename;
  - its own undo history;
  - the Library panel;
  - `get_library` and `update_library`.
- **Notes (08.3):**
  - a new node type (`note_N`): a point, text, an optional short label (a flag), a color, and a status of open or done;
  - the Note tool (`N`);
  - open notes in every outline.
- **Entities (08.4 and 08.5):**
  - entity definitions stored like scenes, with their own history;
  - instances (`instance_N`);
  - Make entity, placing instances, swapping an instance's entity, and Detach;
  - holes through instances;
  - Edit entity mode;
  - a default `human` entity in every project;
  - `make_entity` and `detach_instances`.

### Out (deliberately deferred or dropped)

- **The review loop** (`render_view`: the agent looks at renders of its own work): phase 09. See §14.
- **The array tool** (circle, grid, stack, noise): phase 10.
- **Validators** (reachability, softlocks, from plan 00): later. The walk render in 09 gives a visual check first.
- **Per-instance changes** beyond position, rotation and name: no scale, color or description on an instance. A different size means a different entity.
- **Nested prefabs:** a definition can't contain instances.
- **Mirrored instances:** mirroring moves an instance and mirrors its rotation, but doesn't flip the entity (§7).
- **Notes with an area:** a note is a point, and a radius goes in its text.
- **Notes inside entity definitions.**
- **A library shared across projects.**
- **A text reference to an entity** (a third sigil). An entity's name in plain text is enough for now.
- **The agent opening documents.** The human still opens scenes and entities. The agent makes entities from shapes it draws (`make_entity`) and edits a definition only while the human has it open.

