## 3. Naming and data

| type | ID | fields |
|---|---|---|
| `group` | `group_N` | new: `description?`, `tags?` |
| `box`, `cylinder`, `freeform`, `ramp` | unchanged | new: `tags?` |
| `line` | `line_N` | unchanged (a line is an annotation, and it has no tags) |
| `note` | `note_N` | new: `x`, `y`, `z`, `text`, `label?`, `color`, `status`, `name?`, `parent?`, `locked?`, `hidden?`, `createdBy` |
| `instance` | `instance_N` | new: `entity`, `x`, `y`, `z`, `rotation`, `name?`, `parent?`, `locked?`, `hidden?`, `createdBy` |

- **Every new field is optional,** or has a default where it's required. Old scenes load unchanged.
- **ID counters:** `nextId` gains `note` and `instance`, which default to 1.
- **Counts:** `3 rooms · 2 volumes · 2 holes · 1 ramp · 4 instances · 1 note · 1 group`, in the info-label and in `get_scene`. A done note isn't counted.
- **Tags** are library names (`"climbable"`, stored without the `#`). They're kept in the order given, without duplicates.

### The data folder

```
projects/<project>/
  project.json               name, description, createdAt           (unchanged)
  library.json               seq, tags, skills, seeded               (new, 08.2)
  library-history.jsonl      the library's history log               (new, 08.2)
  rules/design-guide.md      the design guide                        (new, 08.2)
  entities/<entity>/         a definition, laid out like a scene      (08.4)
    entity.json              name, description, tags, createdAt, seq, nextId, nodes
    history.jsonl            its own history log
    editor.json              its camera and selection
  scenes/<scene>/...         unchanged
```

- **`entities/` and `rules/` are folders that already exist** empty in every project (plan 04 reserved `rules/` for the design guide). `abilities/` is no longer created, because skills live in `library.json`. Existing empty `abilities/` folders are left alone. Remove it from `SEMANTIC_FOLDERS`.
- **A definition's ID** is a slug of its name at creation (`tree-tall`), like a scene's. Renaming changes only its `name`, so instances never break.
- **A project with no `library.json`** reads as an empty library.

